From 67f7fe1e15396f92bdf866a45489ccbbdb35fa08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:06:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(ui): GPU lib tests take one process-wide lock

The camcraft-ui lib tests that make a wgpu instance (the headless run,
the adapter probe, and six report-door tests whose screenshot request
starts egui_kittest's wgpu renderer) ran in parallel test threads. On
Windows 11 the test process ended at a random test with
STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION. Each of these tests now takes a poison-tolerant
test-only lock first, so the GPU is used by one test at a time. Three
new tests pin the lock and that each GPU test takes it.

Test code only; the product path makes one instance at a time.

Refs #3589

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
